  "caption": "Quinn reached for the top shelf and the shoulder said no. Then came one-armed hair-washing and a scary diagram online.\n\nPain when reaching overhead is usually an overloaded, sensitised rotator cuff. The old idea of a bone pinching a tendon has largely been replaced, and cuff changes on scans are common in shoulders that don't hurt at all.\n\nWhat often helps: progressive cuff strengthening over 8–12 weeks, gentle overhead movement rather than avoiding it completely, easing back any recent load spike, and a pillow under the sore arm at night. Posture plays a smaller part than many people think.\n\nGet it checked if there's real weakness, a fall or dislocation, sudden loss of movement, or no change after weeks of good rehab.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
